<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chronicle of Alfonso III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chronicle of Alfonso III is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> chronicle written at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iii-of-asturias">Alfonso III of Asturias</a> in the late ninth century, surviving in two versions. Continuing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isidore-of-seville">Isidore of Seville</a>'s history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a>, it covers the kings from Wamba in 672 to the death of Ordoño I in 866. It is the main source for the story of Pelagius and Covadonga and presents the Asturian kings as heirs of the Visigothic monarchy.</p></div>
